  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1207 AM CDT Sat May 9 2026\n\nA low pressure system will continue moving east across western\nTexas on Saturday and Sunday. This system will coincide with a\nstrong cold frontal passage arriving during the early afternoon\nhours of Sunday. These two features combined will provide a high \nchance (70-80%) for thunderstorms to develop ahead of, and along, \nthe cold frontal boundary. Much of the CAMs and other models are \ndepicting some initial scattered thunderstorms that merge into \nmore of a line of thunderstorm during Sunday evening. Conditions \nare favorable for strong to severe thunderstorms as this activity \nmoves through. The Storm Prediction Center has outlooked most of \nour area in a Slight/Enhanced Risk for severe weather during this\ntimeframe. Large hail and damaging winds are the main concerns. \nPlease make sure to check back on this severe weather potential \nfor changes and potential updates.\n\nAfterwards, high pressure redevelops across the region. Expect\nhigh temperatures to make a return to the middle to upper 90s.\nSome locations may even reach into the triple digits towards the\nmiddle and end of this week. No chance for rain is included in the\nforecast for the Tuesday through Friday timeframe of next week.",
